\f4\fs26 Cracker did not see the combination of punches that rained upon him in the seconds after Sarah heard the happy news. He was knocked out after the first fist struck his chin, the rest were just for good measure. \
\'93You rapist!\'94 Sarah yelled through a torrent of tears as Cracker came back to consciousness. \'93I\'92m pregnant! To you? You disgust me.\'94 How he managed to do it without waking her she did not know. She could not remember any chance he had to drug her. Maybe a patch? \'93My DNA mixed with yours?\'94 She began to gag. She had been feeling nauseous for a while and thinking back she had, during that time, found herself obsessively cleaning her apartment and habitually antiquing on the link. It suddenly made some sense.\
\'93I\'92ve only known you a week or so. I couldn\'92t possibly involved.\'94 Cracker hoped she was more that a few weeks along.\
\'93The body begins to produce human chorionic gonadotropin about 5 or so days after the fertilised egg is attached to the uterine wall. The scan shows cell reproduction and growth at about 7 to 10 days. The timings don\'92t seem to fit exactly, but they are within range for human development. Cracker, I don\'92t think I can\'92t defend you on this one.\'94 Kathy Logan took off her patch and sighed. \'93This is going to mess up my buzz, mate.\'94\
\'93No, No. Wait. I did not touch you. How do you know it wasn\'92t Johnny-boy?\'94 Cracker was desperate. \
\'93He was injured and unconscious.\'94 Sarah spat vitriol back at him.\
\'93Well ladies and gentlemen, there appears to be another contender for father of the year. How will we get to the bottom of this little conundrum? If only there was a way to find out who the father is. Oh that\'92s right, I have a DNA-sequencer. I will just have to get a small sample and we will have an answer.\'94 Kathy was feeling better now and slipped the patch back on. Her money was on the other creep, whoever he was. She knew Cracker and he was not that type. He could have taken advantage of her on any number of occasions, but had never crossed that line. Cracker was an enigma to Dr Logan, a paradox of amoral criminality and Victorian decency. \'93Just a quick jab, Sarah.\'94\
The sequencer was loaded with the unborn child\'92s tissue sample and set to chug away for about 10 minutes as it checked, re-checked and checked the data again. \
\'93This is really weird, I mean really weird.\'94 She could not hold back a hysterical laugh. \'93So strange. Only you could bring me something like this, Cracker.\'94\
Kathy\'92s amusement did not reduce Cracker\'92s anxiety. His heart was pounding loudly and hot flushes pulsed across his body, leaving his face and neck a blotchy bright red. He wondered whether he had suffered from some memory lapse or had indulged in some form of sleep-fucking. 
\f5\i Sleep-fucking? Is that a thing?
\f4\i0  He knew their way no way he was involved in the conception, but he was still petrified. He held his breath, crossed his fingers and hoped.\
\'93Cracker, you are not the father.\'94 \
\'93Thank the Dawkins.\'94 Cracker blurted out, not knowing why. \'93Hell yeah! I told you, Sarah.\'94 He raised both arms jubilantly and immediately regretted the little act of celebratory anger, but did not think to apologise.\
\'93Well, you are hooked into the data-base, who is the father?\'94 Sarah could not yet bring herself to believe the result. She had found it very easy to blame Cracker, but was finding extreme difficulty in withdrawing the accusation. Her womanhood had been assailed at its very core and the sick feeling of violation would not retreat.\
 \
\'93I can\'92t tell you that either. What I can tell you Sarah is that you are not the mother.\'94 Kathy was enjoying herself, she loved when a mystery presented itself.\
